HWG_TOOL_DESCRIPTION = "Compile or run a .hwg flowchart file. A .hwg graph wires multiple .hwo workflows together with conditions and loop-backs. Syntax: (find.hwo)#find# declares a node bound to a .hwo file (its body is the whole workflow in that file); !(review.hwo)#review# marks a manual (human) node; #from# -> #to# is an edge; #review# -> { on: PASS } #report# is a conditional edge; #review# -> { on: FAIL, maxLoops: 2 } #analyze# is a bounded loop-back; (schedule) { start: \"09:00\", days: [\"Mon\",\"Fri\"], tz: \"Asia/Shanghai\" } sets a recurring schedule. ``` ... ``` is a comment block. Node ids must be unique; every edge endpoint must reference a declared node; a node with more than one outgoing edge is a branch and every branch edge must carry `on:`; a self-loop must carry `maxLoops`. action=compile parses and validates without executing; action=run walks the graph from the start node, executing each node's .hwo file in order. After a node runs, its verdict (from agent_return, or PASS/FAIL by default) is matched against outgoing edge conditions to pick the next node. Manual nodes pause the run."
HWG_SYNTAX = "HWG flowchart syntax:\n  (file.hwo)#name#              a node bound to a .hwo workflow file\n  !(file.hwo)#name#             a manual (human) node — run pauses here\n  #from# -> #to#                an edge from one node to another\n  #from# -> { on: PASS } #to#             conditional edge (taken when condition matches)\n  #from# -> { on: FAIL, maxLoops: 2 } #to#  bounded loop-back (retries up to N times)\n  (schedule) { start: \"09:00\", days: [\"Mon\"], tz: \"Asia/Shanghai\" }   recurring schedule\n  ``` ... ```                   comment block\n  ->                            no-op separator (ignored)\n\nRULES:\n  1. Every node MUST bind a .hwo file — write (file.hwo)#name#, never a bare #name# as a declaration.\n  2. Node ids must be unique across the whole graph.\n  3. A bare #name# only appears as an edge endpoint: #from# -> #to#.\n  4. A node with >1 outgoing edge is a branch — every outgoing edge must carry `on:`.\n  5. A self-loop (#a# -> #a#) must carry `maxLoops` to bound the loop.\n\nExample — research → review with a retry loop:\n  ``` find, analyze, review; loop back on FAIL, max 2 retries ```\n  (find.hwo)#find#\n  (analyze.hwo)#analyze#\n  !(review.hwo)#review#\n  (report.hwo)#report#\n\n  #find# -> #analyze#\n  #analyze# -> #review#\n  #review# -> { on: PASS } #report#\n  #review# -> { on: FAIL, maxLoops: 2 } #analyze#"
